143
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:26,640
Their positions in this array define the
scales starting at 0.

144
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:32,334
So with 3 levels the score runs from 0 to 2
and this is a rating not a

145
00:09:32,334 --> 00:09:36,971
percentage let's set the state the customer
politely asks

146
00:09:36,971 --> 00:09:41,120
for help with a larger size let's run this
request.

147
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:46,628
the score is 0 hour calm level and the
customer has a problem with the shoes but

148
00:09:46,628 --> 00:09:51,091
they're not expressing frustration right
this question measures

149
00:09:51,091 --> 00:09:55,200
their tone separately from the issue that
needs resolving.

150
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:57,840
Let's try 1 where the customer is angry.

151
00:09:57,840 --> 00:10:01,752
This customer says they've contacted the
store 3 times, they're furious,

152
00:10:01,752 --> 00:10:03,600
they're never shopping here again.

153
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:05,375
So this score is a 2,

154
00:10:05,375 --> 00:10:11,459
which is our highest level that it describes
strong anger or a threat to

155
00:10:11,459 --> 00:10:18,388
stop shopping with the store um and this
message contains both so within our code,

156
00:10:18,388 --> 00:10:23,120
we can guide our agent on what to do next
